th: FY25 actual 13.4% [Arithmetic] \u2192 10%/8%/7%/7%/7% [Assumption \u2014 long-run multi-strategy median]; fixed income: $3.8B at 4.7% YTM [Actual] declining ~25bp/yr [Assumption].\n- Tax 8%: [Assumption] pack withheld effective rate; Bermuda 0% base blended with US/UK subs.\n- Shares declining ~2%/yr on $137M buyback authority [Actual] + ongoing buybacks at ~$30\u201336 [Assumption].\n\nValuation outputs:\n\n(1) Residual income (RI) on book value \u2014 B0 = $28.91 (BVPS 6/30/26 [Actual]); cost of equity = 10.0%; terminal ROE = 10% (= cost of equity; no terminal excess value):\nRI PVs: 2026 $2.24 + 2027 $1.31 + 2028 $0.67 + 2029 $0.27 + 2030 $0.10 = $4.59\n\u2192 IV = $28.91 + $4.59 = $33.50 [Estimate]\n\n(2) Justified P/B (Gordon): P/B = (ROE \u2212 g)/(r \u2212 g) = (0.115 \u2212 0.03)/(0.10 \u2212 0.03) = 1.21\u00d7\nApplied to forward book (YE27E ~$35.80) discounted 1.5y @ 10%:\nIV \u2248 1.21 \u00d7 35.8 / 1.153 = $37.5 [Estimate]\n\n(3) Normalized EPS: mid-cycle ROE 11.5% \u00d7 ~$33 avg book \u2248 $3.80; normal multiple 8\u201311\u00d7 (re/insurer mid-cycle, rate-sensitive, > beta-1 business) \u2192 $32\u201344; central $38 [Assumption]\n\n(4) Tornado (top-3 variables \u00b11\u03c3):\n- Terminal/mid-cycle ROE \u00b13pts \u2192 IV \u00b1 $9 (dominant)\n- 2028 combined ratio \u00b12pts \u2192 IV \u00b1 $4\n- Two Sigma cumulative return over 3 yrs \u00b110pts vs base \u2192 IV \u00b1 $3.5\n\nIV CENTRAL: **$36** [Estimate] (50% CI $32\u201341; 80% CI $27\u201347)\n\nDiscount-rate derivation (spelled out): Rf = 4.7% (10Y UST [Actual]); ERP = 5.0% [Assumption \u2014 standard post-2008 Damodaran range]; beta: vendor reports 0.437 [Aggregator \u2014 unreliable window/benchmark]; fundamental beta for a re/insurer with catastrophe + Two Sigma exposure = 1.0 [Assumption]; no debt adjustment needed (net cash). Ke = 4.7% + 1.0\u00d75.0% + 0.3% size premium = **10.0%** [Assumption]. I also tested 9.0% and 11.0%; IV range midpoints $38 and $33 respectively \u2014 conclusion (fairly valued) is robust.\n\nReverse DCF / market-implied check: Price $34.96 \u00f7 BVPS $28.91 = 1.21\u00d7 \u2192 market-implied *perpetual* ROE \u2248 11.5% (using r=10%, g=3%). The market is NOT extrapolating peak 22% ROE; it is pricing rapid normalization to the low-teens. My base case fades to ~10\u201311% by 2029\u201330. Market-implied terminal ROE is only ~0.5\u20131.5pt above mine \u2192 the market's expectation is rational, and the expected excess return is near zero.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\nSECTION 3.5. SECOND-ORDER EFFECTS\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\nStep 3.5-1. Competitive response: If HG's Hamilton Select grows aggressively, Kinsale/Arch \u2014 with lower cost structures \u2014 can undercut on price without moving their own margins below acceptable ROE. Score: -2 (negative for HG's E&S growth plan).\nStep 3.5-2. Reflexivity: Positive loop (high BVPS/rating) supports growth via A\u2212 \u2192 A upgrade and cheaper capital. Negative loop muted by $6.1B liquidity; but a Two Sigma drawdown > 10% would hit both earnings and the \"sophisticated asset manager\" narrative, and complicate the already-soft market. Score: -1.\nStep 3.5-3. Customer/flow evolution: Hamilton Select expansion into E&S middle market via new distribution is the growth engine; as penetration grows, E&S margins converge to the market's pricing cycle. LTV/CAC not published [Unconfirmed].\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\nSECTION 4. SCENARIOS (BAYESIAN)\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\nPrior (Layer 1.5 base rates): 30\u201340% probability of \u226540% drawdown within 3 years from a cyclical peak; casualty reserve-failure base rate > 50%.\nUpdate triggers (H1-26): CR 95% vs 86.8% prior year (+8.2pts) [Actual]; casualty charge $16.1M [Actual]; two segment GPW +21.8%/+11.9% [Actual]; attritional loss ratio up 1.3pts to 55.7% [Estimate \u2014 web brief citing company data]. Posterior is roughly neutral-to-slightly-bearish relative to prior: the earnings delivery is real, but the margin erosion is visible.\n\nScenarios (probabilities sum to 100%; 12-month price targets, discounted to T0):\n\n| Scenario | Prob | Narrative | Price today | 12-m range |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Bull | 20% | Pricing holds (Munich-Re view); casualty stays firm; Two Sigma +10%/yr; CR ~93\u201395; ROE 15\u201318%. | $44 | $43\u201352 |\n| Base | 45% | Gradual softening; CR 94\u219298; ROE fades to ~10\u201311% by 2030; buybacks continue. | $38 | $35\u201341 |\n| Bear | 25% | Accelerating soft market (property \u221215%/yr; casualty negative by 2028); reserve charges continue; ROE 5\u20138%. | $28 | $25\u201331 |\n| Crash | 10% | Industry cat loss year + Two Sigma \u221210% + reserve charge; BVPS \u221210%; ROE 1\u20133%. | $22 | $19\u201324 |\n\nExpected price = 0.20\u00d744 + 0.45\u00d738 + 0.25\u00d728 + 0.10\u00d722 = **$35.1** [Arithmetic]\nExpected 12-month total return = ($35.1 + ~$0.20 dividends \u2212 $34.96)/$34.96 \u2248 **+1%**. 50% CI: $30\u201340; 80% CI: $24\u201348.\nMargin of safety: (IV $36 \u2212 price $34.96)/$36 = **+2.9% \u2192 LIMITED**.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\nSECTION 4.5. HORIZON ARBITRAGE\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\nMarket-implied horizon: the 1.21\u00d7 P/B embeds an 11.5% perpetual ROE \u2014 i.e., the market is looking through the current 22% ROE and pricing a ~2-year fade to mid-cycle. My explicit fade reaches 10.4% only by 2030. The spread = My horizon (3\u20135 years) vs Market horizon (2 years). At T0, the market's 2-year fade is if anything *faster* than my 4\u20135-year fade for 2027\u201329, meaning there is NO horizon arbitrage at current price. A trade only exists if one believes HG's 2026\u201327 underwriting margins hold at 94\u201395% while the market prices 97% \u2014 that is a modest, low-margin bet, not a multi-year edge.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\nSECTION 5. CONVICTION & POSITION SIZING\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\nStep 5-1. Conviction score (0\u20133 each):\n1. Business quality: 2 (narrow moat, excellent execution, sub-scale)\n2. Valuation attractiveness: 1 (MoS ~3%; IV \u2248 price)\n3. Macro alignment: 2 (rates high = NII tailwind; pricing cycle = headwind; net neutral)\n4. Thesis clarity (measurable KPIs): 3 (CR, attritional loss ratio, Two Sigma returns, BVPS, GPW, reserve charges)\n5. Execution traceability: 3 (BVPS +64% since listing; Q1/Q2 beats; clear guidance)\nTotal = 11/15 \u2192 HIGH (raw)\nStep 5-2. Decay: \u22121 point per 6 months without new confirming evidence. IPO tailwind is spent; no new confirming evidence in Q2-26 (margins compressed) \u2192 apply \u22121 \u2192 **10/15 (HIGH)**.\nStep 5-3. Macro/sector headwind (cycle softening) \u2192 cap weight at 50% of normal High conviction band (4\u20136%) \u2192 **max 3%**.\n\nStep 6.5 Kelly sizing: Expected excess return \u2248 \u22121.5% (scenario-weighted) \u2192 **Kelly fraction \u2264 0%**. No new position; if held as a legacy position, size \u2264 2% for monitoring only. (Reconciliation with Layer 5 3% cap: gap = 1pp, not >20pp, so no re-analysis required; the binding constraint is Kelly = 0.)\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550