uate [Actual \u2014 Q2 call]; (2) reserves adequate? \u2014 Watch item: $16.1M casualty charge from a 2018 single loss in Q2-26 [Actual]; (3) balance sheet liquid? \u2014 Yes, $6.1B invested.\n\nStep 2-4. Financial strength scorecard (company-reported basis):\n- Revenue (GPW) growth: FY25 +21% to $2.9B; FY26 guide low double-digit [Actual]\n- Net premiums earned: FY25 $2.1B (+21.6%) [Actual]\n- Combined ratio: FY24 91.3%; FY25 92.9%; Q2-26 95.0% (incl. 8.5pt cats) [Actual] \u2192 trending toward mid-90s as cycle softens\n- Net income: FY25 $577M (+44%); Q1-26 $134M; Q2-26 $144M [Actual]\n- ROAE: FY25 22%; Q2-26 annualized 21% [Actual]\n- BVPS: $28.91 (6/30/26); +8.5% adj. YTD; +64% since 2023 listing [Actual]\n- NII: FY25 $512M; Q2-26 $141M [Actual]\n- Debt: $150M LT debt + $7M leases; ~$1.2B cash; $6.1B total invested [Actual/Estimate]\n- Judgment: EXCELLENT at cyclical peak; ADEQUATE on normalized basis.\n\nStep 2-5. Capital allocation scorecard (0\u20133 each):\n1. Buyback efficiency: 2 \u2014 $93.4M buybacks in 2025 [Estimate \u2014 research brief] at ~$26\u201333 (below 1.3x book = okay); $42M YTD 2026 + $137M remaining [Actual]. Not aggressive at peak; fine.\n2. M&A track record: 2 \u2014 Hamilton Select expansion via internal capital, no value-destructive M&A; track record short.\n3. Capex efficiency: 3 \u2014 negligible capex; capital deployed into underwriting at 20%+ ROE through 2025.\n4. Reinvestment vs payout mix: 2 \u2014 balance of growth + buybacks + special dividend ($2.00 declared FY25) [Actual].\n5. Guidance accuracy: 3 \u2014 FY25 GPW +21% vs guidance; Q1/Q2-26 beats (EPS $1.31 vs $1.23 consensus; operating 24% ROAE); no guidance withdrawals [Actual/Estimate].\nInsider bonus: CEO term extended to Dec-2029 [Actual] but no large open-market buying; 5.07% insider ownership [Aggregator]. Net +0.\nTotal: 12/15 \u2192 GOOD.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u