\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\nForecast path \u2014 every driver is sourced. Period 2026 = guided year; 2027\u20132030 = cycle-normalization assumptions (clearly labeled).\n\n| (per share, $) | 2026E | 2027E | 2028E | 2029E | 2030E |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| NPE ($B) | 2.33 | 2.49 | 2.59 | 2.67 | 2.74 |\n| Combined ratio (%) | 94.0 | 95.5 | 97.0 | 98.0 | 98.0 |\n| Underwriting income ($M) | 140 | 112 | 78 | 53 | 55 |\n| Net invest. income ($M) | 480 | 440 | 420 | 410 | 400 |\n| Pre-tax income ($M) | ~598 | ~530 | ~476 | ~441 | ~433 |\n| Net income ($M) @ 8% tax [Assumption] | 550 | 488 | 438 | 406 | 398 |\n| Diluted shares (M) | 99 | 97 | 95 | 93 | 92 |\n| EPS ($) | 5.55 | 5.03 | 4.60 | 4.35 | 4.34 |\n| ROE (%) | ~18 | ~14.5 | ~12.4 | ~11.0 | ~10.4 |\n\nDriver sourcing:\n- NPE 2026 = 2025 $2.1B [Actual] \u00d7 1.11 (guidance \"low double-digit GPW growth\" [Actual \u2014 Q2-26], NPE grows slightly slower than GPW). 2027\u201330 growth 7%\u21922.5%: [Assumption] based on AM Best \"stable\" outlook, CIAB \"premium decreases accelerate in Q2-26,\" Munich Re \"Jan-27 renewals largely upheld,\" RenRe \"changing, not soft\" [all Actual industry sources] \u2014 pricing softens but does not collapse.\n- Combined ratio 2026 = 94.0: [Assumption] Q2-26 actual 95.0 (incl 8.5pt cats) [Actual]; Q1-26 better (operating ROAE 24%); full-year midpoint. 2027\u201330 drift to 98: [Assumption] reflects property rate softening + casualty reserve creep; guided attritional targets (54.5%/56%) [Actual] and actual FY25 attritional 54.4% [Actual] are held ~flat to slightly up in my model.\n- Net investment income 2026 $480M: between the unsustainable H1-26 run-rate (~$565M annualized [Arithmetic]) and normalized ($410M). Two Sigma path: FY25 actual 13.4% [Arithmetic] \u2192 10%/8%/7%/7%/7% [Assumption \u2014 long-run multi-strategy median]; fixed income: $3.8B at 4.7% YTM [Actual] declining ~25bp/yr [Assumption].\n- Tax 8%: [Assumption] pack withheld effective rate; Bermuda 0% base blended with US/UK subs.\n- Shares declining ~2%/yr on $137M buyback authority [Actual] + ongoing buybacks at ~$30\u201336 [Assumption].\n\nValuation outputs:\n\n(1) Residual income (RI) on book value \u2014 B0 = $28.91 (BVPS 6/30/26 [Actual]); cost of equity = 10.0%; terminal ROE = 10% (= cost of equity; no terminal excess value):\nRI PVs: 2026 $2.24 + 2027 $1.31 + 2028 $0.67 + 2029 $0.27 + 2030 $0.10 = $4.59\n\u2192 IV = $28.91 + $4.59 = $33.50 [Estimate]\n\n(2) Justified P/B (Gordon): P/B = (ROE \u2212 g)/(r \u2212 g) = (0.115 \u2212 0.03)/(0.10 \u2212 0.03) = 1.21\u00d7\nApplied to forward book (YE27E ~$35.80) discounted 1.5y @ 10%:\nIV \u2248 1.21 \u00d7 35.8 / 1.153 = $37.5 [Estimate]\n\n(3) Normalized EPS: mid-cycle ROE 11.5% \u00d7 ~$33 avg book \u2248 $3.80; normal multiple 8\u201311\u00d7 (re/insurer mid-cycle, rate-sensitive, > beta-1 business) \u2192 $32\u201344; central $38 [Assumption]\n\n(4) Tornado (top-3 variables \u00b11\u03c3):\n- Terminal/mid-cycle ROE \u00b13pts \u2192 IV \u00b1 $9 (dominant)\n- 2028 combined ratio \u00b12pts \u2192 IV \u00b1 $4\n- Two Sigma cumulative return over 3 yrs \u00b110pts vs base \u2192 IV \u00b1 $3.5\n\nIV CENTRAL: **$36** [Estimate] (50% CI $32\u201341; 80% CI $27\u201347)\n\nDiscount-rate derivation (spelled out): Rf = 4.7% (10Y UST [Actual]); ERP = 5.0% [Assumption \u2014 standard post-2008 Damodaran range]; beta: vendor reports 0.437 [Aggregator \u2014 unreliable window/benchmark]; fundamental beta for a re/insurer with catastrophe + Two Sigma exposure = 1.0 [Assumption]; no debt adjustment needed (net cash). Ke = 4.7% + 1.0\u00d75.0% + 0.3% size premium = **10.0%** [Assumption]. I also tested 9.0% and 11.0%; IV range midpoints $38 and $33 respectively \u2014 conclusion (fairly valued) is robust.\n\nReverse DCF / market-implied check: Price $34.96 \u00f7 BVPS $28.91 = 1.21\u00d7 \u2192 market-implied *perpetual* ROE \u2248 11.5% (using r=10%, g=3%). The market is NOT extrapolating peak 22% ROE; it is pricing rapid normalization to the low-teens. My base case fades to ~10\u201311% by 2029\u201330. Market-implied terminal ROE is only ~0.5\u20131.5pt above mine \u2192 the market's expectation is rational, and the expected excess return is near zero.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\nSECTION 3.5. SECOND-ORDER EFFECTS\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\nStep 3.5-1. Competitive response: If HG's Hamilton Select grows aggressively, Kinsale/Arch \u2014 with lower cost structures \u2014 can undercut on price without moving their own margins below acceptable ROE. Score: -2 (negative for HG's E&S growth plan).\nStep 3.5-2. Reflexivity: Positive loop (high BVPS/rating) supports growth via A\u2212 \u2192 A upgrade and cheaper capital. Negative loop muted by $6.1B liquidity; but a Two Sigma drawdown > 10% would hit both earnings and the \"sophisticated asset manager\" narrative, and complicate the already-soft market. Score: -1.\nStep 3.5-3. Customer/flow